BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 6210 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: SCIN010089012026
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice Surya Kant & Justice K.V. Viswanathan

PARTIES:
Phoenix ARC Private Limited \(Asset Reconstruction Company\)
... Petitioner\(s\) / Appellant\(s\)
Versus
Ketan Patel & Anr. \(Borrowers\)
... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Securitisation and Reconstruction of Financial Assets and Enforcement of Security Interest Act 2002

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
SARFAESI Act Section 13\(2\), SARFAESI Act Section 13\(4\), SARFAESI Act Section 17

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
SARFAESI, Asset Reconstruction, Secured Creditor, DRT Jurisdiction, Non-Performing Asset

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
High Court entertained Article 226 writ petition and stayed SARFAESI auction of secured asset despite borrower bypassing DRT under Section 17.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
Can High Court exercise writ jurisdiction under Article 226 to stall auction proceedings under Section 13\(4\) of SARFAESI Act?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
High Courts should not entertain writ petitions challenging SARFAESI actions when effective statutory remedy exists before DRT under Section 17.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Civil Appeal Allowed; High Court order staying SARFAESI auction quashed; Section 17 DRT remedy is exclusive.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice Surya Kant & Justice K.V. Viswanathan
Supreme Court of India
[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]
